  },
  {
   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "Changes in shot mix could be confounded by various factors not accounted for by simply observing lineup changes, such as opponent defense, game state (score, clock), coaching strategy, or individual player performance variations. Isolating the 'offensive five itself' effect is challenging."
  },
  {
   "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
   "text": "Defining 'shot mix' and reliably measuring its change across different lineups, especially for short stints, can be difficult. The chosen granularity of shot mix (e.g., restricted area vs. mid-range vs. 3-point) and the minimum number of possessions required for a stable estimate will impact reliability."
  }
 ],
