  "multiplicity": "Given that shot mix will be broken down into multiple categories (e.g., 2-point, 3-point, restricted area, mid-range) and potentially multiple lineup changes are examined, False Discovery Rate (FDR) control (e.g., Benjamini-Hochberg procedure) will be applied to adjust p-values for multiple comparisons.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis will be considered supported if a statistically significant and practically meaningful change (e.g., >2 percentage points change in a primary shot category) in at least one key shot mix category is consistently observed following a change in the offensive five, after controlling for confounding factors and adjusting for multiplicity. The effect should be robust across different model specifications and pass falsification tests. If no such change is detected or if the effect is not robust, the hypothesis will be rejected or deemed untestable/uncertain.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular season and playoffs play-by-play (action type, sub-type, clock, period, score, player, shot distance and result), substitution rotation intervals, starters, defensive matchup minutes and partial possessions, box-score summary. Derived play-type possession records (initiator, play type, points) in a graph database built from the play-by-play."
 }

